<p>On the basis of exchange rates from 21-23 June, the largest average RMG is that of sterling at 4.768 per cent. This creates a negative threshold of -0.232 per cent (5 - 4.768). Since the average RMGs for Belgium, Germany, Holland, France and Austria are all below this level they are currently forecast to devalue on 1 July, the start of the next monitoring period. All other green rates are forecast to remain unchanged from 1 July.</p>
